  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nPrecipitation trends are looking up for the Panhandles as we \napproach the second week of September. Global models are forecasting \nanother toasty weekend for the area as an Omega Block pattern sets \nup through early next week. While this still promotes highs in the \n90s to triple digits, this does \"dirty up\" the ridge enough to allow \nfor occasional rain chances through the week. The block likely \nbegins to break down by midweek, but model agreement drastically \ngoes down the proverbial drain. Long range guidance is greatly \nstruggling to decide how to evolve the upper ridge as deep troughing \ntakes over the western CONUS, but ensemble members suggest that the \nsynoptic pattern could favor wetter outcomes. Even though confidence \nis low on the precipitation potential, a very gradual \"cooling \ntrend\" is looking more attainable. Perhaps we could even see high \ntemperatures in the 80s return by mid month.\n\nHarrel",
